@startuml KTOB_14_state_reading
title KTOB - ReadingExperience Lifecycle (not LibraryEntry shelf)
[*] --> CURRENTLY_READING : start actual reading
[*] --> FINISHED : historical import (explicit)
[*] --> PAUSED : historical import (explicit)
[*] --> DID_NOT_FINISH : historical import (explicit)
CURRENTLY_READING --> PAUSED : pause
PAUSED --> CURRENTLY_READING : resume
CURRENTLY_READING --> FINISHED : finish
CURRENTLY_READING --> DID_NOT_FINISH : abandon
PAUSED --> FINISHED : finish retrospectively
PAUSED --> DID_NOT_FINISH : abandon
FINISHED --> [*] : reading concluded; record retained
DID_NOT_FINISH --> [*] : reading concluded; record retained
note right of CURRENTLY_READING
At most one CURRENTLY_READING or PAUSED
experience per library entry at a time.
end note
note bottom of FINISHED
WANT_TO_READ is only a derived LibraryEntry shelf.
A reread creates a new experience; prior one is retained.
Terminal FINISHED and DID_NOT_FINISH cannot be reopened.
Dates, rating, progress and edition can still be corrected.
Rating 1..5 in half-steps and progress 0..100 are
optional and do not automatically trigger status transitions.
end note
@enduml
